<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <%# No engineTrackingCode on this page: engine.js only receives the visitor code and the consent %>
  <%- include("partials/kameleoon", { siteCode, visitorCode, consent }) %>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Server-side tracking | Kameleoon hybrid starter kit</title>
  <%- include("partials/style") %>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <nav>
    <a href="/server-tracking" class="current">Server-side tracking</a>
    <a href="/engine-tracking">Engine-side tracking</a>
  </nav>

  <h1>Server-side tracking</h1>
  <p>A hybrid page. The Node.js SDK evaluates one feature flag and reports its exposure.
    engine.js receives the visitor code and consent, so both sides identify the same visitor.</p>

  <h2>What happened for this request</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><code>getVisitorCode()</code> read or created the visitor code.</li>
    <li><code>setLegalConsent()</code> gave the SDK the consent choice, if there is one.</li>
    <% if (variation) { %>
      <li><code>getVariation()</code> evaluated <code><%= featureKey %></code> and reported the exposure from the server.</li>
    <% } else { %>
      <li><code>getVariation()</code> could not evaluate <code><%= featureKey %></code>, so nothing was reported.</li>
    <% } %>
    <li>The page gave the same visitor code and consent to engine.js.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Result</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Visitor code</th><td><code><%= visitorCode %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Consent</th><td><code><%= consent %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Feature key</th><td><code><%= featureKey %></code></td></tr>
    <% if (variation) { %>
      <tr><th>Variation</th><td><code><%= variation.key %></code><%= variation.name ? ` (${variation.name})` : "" %></td></tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Variables</th>
        <td>
          <% if (variation.variables.size === 0) { %>
            None
          <% } else { %>
            <% for (const [key, variable] of variation.variables) { %>
              <div><code><%= key %></code> = <code><%= JSON.stringify(variable.value) %></code></div>
            <% } %>
          <% } %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    <% } else { %>
      <tr>
        <th>Variation</th>
        <td>Default experience. The flag was not evaluated: the key is unknown, the flag is
          disabled in this environment, or the project blocks experiments because consent is
          denied. The server log has the reason.</td>
      </tr>
    <% } %>
    <tr><th>Exposure reported by</th><td><%= variation ? "Node.js SDK" : "Nobody: the flag was not evaluated" %></td></tr>
  </table>

  <%- include("partials/consent", { consent }) %>
</main>
</body>
</html>
